        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vivian Pinn\n- Organizations: Harvard University, Tufts University, Howard University College of Medicine, Tufts College, Christian Universalists\n- Places: Massachusetts, Washington, D.C.\n- Roles: assistant dean of student and minority affairs, chair of the Department of Pathology\n\nFacts:\n- Tufts College was founded in 1852 by Christian Universalists who had worked for years to open a nonsectarian institution of higher learning.\n- Vivian Pinn previously taught at Harvard University in Massachusetts.\n- Vivian Pinn previously taught at Tufts University in Massachusetts and served there as assistant dean of student and minority affairs.\n- Vivian Pinn previously taught at Howard University College of Medicine in Washington, D.C., and chaired its Department of Pathology.",
